# E337 - Reproducible Autotools bootstrap for a source snapshot with gnulib

id:                     E460
trigger_tool:           conan|configure|autotools|make
phase:                  configuration|compilation|installation|testing
error_signature:        configure: No such file or directory|bootstrap.*failed|aclocal.*not found|automake.*not found|libtoolize.*not found|gnulib.*not found|po/Makefile\.in

severity:               2
category:               portability, build-system, autotools, conan
match_keywords:         Git snapshot, generated configure, Makefile.in, bootstrap, bootstrap.conf, gnulib, automake, libtool, gettext, m4, --skip-po, NLS, source tag, generated files
title:                  Pin gnulib and bootstrap tools when Conan builds an Autotools source snapshot

root_cause:             A Git tag can intentionally omit generated Autotools files and expect a matching gnulib tree plus a complete bootstrap toolchain. Treating the tag as a release archive, using an unrelated gnulib revision, or relying on undeclared host tools makes configure generation and the later recursive build non-reproducible.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes for Autotools projects distributed as Git snapshots or development trees whose bootstrap script imports gnulib and regenerates configure, Makefile.in, or libtool files.
verification_cmd:       Check that the source snapshot and gnulib archive hashes match conandata.yml; before bootstrap record the absence of generated files; run bootstrap with the pinned gnulib path and declared tools; then verify configure, Makefile.in, and required generated headers before configure, make, package, and consumer testing.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           pinned-gnulib-bootstrap-toolchain
rec_description:        Treat the source tag and gnulib revision as one build input. Declare missing bootstrap tools as Conan tool requirements, pass an absolute gnulib path to bootstrap, make NLS/po generation consistent with the recipe, and build generated library outputs before dependent source targets.
rec_command:            conan create . -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-bootstrap

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      approved-prebuilt-autotools-input
fallback_description:   If the CI worker cannot run the required bootstrap tools, use a repository-approved, checksummed generated-file archive produced from the exact source and gnulib revisions. Keep the provenance and regeneration command auditable.
fallback_command:       verify the generated-file archive hash, unpack it into the exact source tree, then run the normal cross configure and build
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          prebuilt-generated-files

forbid_1_pattern:       unrelated.*gnulib|latest.*gnulib|download.*gnulib.*without.*sha256
forbid_1_reason:        Generated files depend on gnulib modules and macros; an unpinned or unrelated revision can silently change configure behavior or generated source contents.
forbid_1_consequence:   Local and CI builds can diverge while the recipe appears to use the same upstream version.
forbid_2_pattern:       --disable-nls.*unconditional.*po/Makefile|skip-po.*without.*consumer
forbid_2_reason:        Disabling NLS must also remove unconditional po generation paths, while package validation still needs a real consumer test.
forbid_2_consequence:   Bootstrap or make fails in po, or a package can pass without proving its public library contract.
forbid_3_pattern:       commit.*generated.*configure|hand-written.*configure|make.*src.*before.*lib
forbid_3_reason:        Generated Autotools files must come from the pinned bootstrap inputs, and dependent source targets need generated library headers and archives first.
forbid_3_consequence:   The recipe becomes stale or fails with missing generated headers/libgnu artifacts.

principles:             P003, P010, P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E007, E041, E058]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

